# Tool Registration – Add-on Architecture

When building a new tool or adding an npm package, follow the pattern in `docs/TOOL-REGISTRATION.md`.

## Quick Reference

- **Single registration point**: `src/app/registered-tools.ts` – add route + tool card here
- **Route data**: Use `data: { hideMainTabBar: true }` for tools with their own tab bar
- **No path coupling**: TabsPage uses `shouldHideMainTabBar(router)` from `@app/shared/utils` – never hardcode tool paths in tabs.page.ts

## Adding a New Tool

1. Add route to `REGISTERED_TOOL_ROUTES` in `registered-tools.ts`
2. Add tool card to `REGISTERED_TOOL_CARDS` in `registered-tools.ts`
3. If the tool has a custom tab bar, include `data: { hideMainTabBar: true }` on the route

Do NOT edit `tabs.page.ts` or `tabs.routes.ts` for new tools – they are driven by `registered-tools.ts`.

